  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 324 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nThe most notable change to the forecast for this issuance is that \nguidance consensus has trended further westward with the placement \nof an upper-level ridge relative to the Middle Mississippi Valley. \nWhile at the start of the period on Tuesday the axis will be \nroughly along the Mississippi River, it will quickly retrograde \nto over the Great Plains by Wednesday. The positioning of this \nridge will place the CWA beneath northwesterly flow and keep the\nridge's thermal component west of the region. The result is \nthat while temperatures are still expected to gradually warm, \nthe degree of warmth has been muted compared to recent previous \nforecasts. The NBM (mid to upper 70s) is still a couple of \ndegrees warmer than the global ensemble members (low to mid \n70s), but at least is now more in line with guidance consensus \nthan as of late. \n\nLate in the period (Saturday), a trough ejects out into the Plains \nand pinches the ridge; however, deterministic and ensemble guidance \nvaries drastically in the phasing of these features. Therefore, \nconfidence in our local weather is very low Saturday into the \nweekend.",
